      "content": "If forced to choose, the prevailing argument within sports science for maintaining competitive integrity prioritizes biological sex as the defining factor in categories. This position strictly argues that physiological differences resulting from sex development create quantifiable and often insurmountable performance gaps. From this viewpoint, the primary function of elite sport is to measure the ceiling of human performance within defined biological parameters.",
